userStories.description:
**Goal** — Introduce the memory note types, constants, frontmatter codec and permanent-push-rejection recognizer.

**Motivation** — The native agent starts every session blank.

**Approach** — A note file is frontmatter between two `---` lines, one `key: value` per line (the `MemoryNote` keys other than `body`, in any order; a value is everything after the first `: `, so a description may itself contain `: `; values are single-line plain scalars, no quoting, no nesting; an unknown key is ignored), then one blank line, then the body. `parseMemoryNote(text)` validates with a zod schema and throws `NaxError` code `MEMORY_NOTE_INVALID` (message names the first bad key) on a missing, unknown-enum or line-break-carrying field; `serializeMemoryNote(note)` writes the keys in the order `id, slug, type, scope, description, source, updatedAt, status`, then `---`, then a blank line, then the body (for an empty body the file ends with `---\n`). The two round-trip.

Example:
```markdown
---
id: mem_01J9X2
slug: replay-budget
type: project
scope: project
description: replay budget stays 2,048 MiB
source: nax-chat
updatedAt: 2026-11-02T08:11:00.000Z
status: active
---

The replay budget stays at 2,048 MiB. Next export append is due ~11-23.
```

A provider that refuses a write for a reason retrying cannot fix throws `NaxError` code `MEMORY_PUSH_REJECTED` (message = the reason); `isMemoryPushRejected(error)` recognises it. Any other throw or a timeout is transient.

**Scope** — In: create types.ts, note.ts and the memory/index.ts barrel; named public exports from src/index.ts, types via export type; regenerate api/nax-agent.api.txt with bun run api:update. All memory-origin NaxErrors have stage memory. Out: write validation/secret refusal (US-002), store persistence (US-003 onward), provider implementations (US-009). Multi-line or quoted frontmatter values and YAML nesting are not supported; values are single-line scalars.

**Interface** —
```ts
export type MemoryNoteType = "user" | "feedback" | "project" | "reference";
export type MemoryScope = "project" | "user";
export type MemoryNoteStatus = "active" | "pending" | "superseded" | "rejected" | "deleted";
export interface MemoryNote {
  readonly id: string;           // provider id, or the clientId of the write until synced
  readonly slug: string;         // MEMORY_SLUG_RE
  readonly type: MemoryNoteType;
  readonly scope: MemoryScope;
  readonly description: string;  // one line, <= MEMORY_DESCRIPTION_MAX_CHARS
  readonly source: string;       // one line, <= 64 chars: "nax-chat" | "nax-run" | "koda-thread" | "human" | "import" | any label
  readonly updatedAt: string;    // ISO 8601
  readonly status: MemoryNoteStatus;
  readonly body: string;         // Markdown, <= MEMORY_NOTE_BODY_MAX_BYTES (UTF-8)
}
export interface MemoryDecision {
  readonly id: string; readonly subject: string; readonly predicate: string;
  readonly object: string; readonly updatedAt: string; readonly status: "active" | "superseded" | "rejected";
}
export interface MemoryHit {
  readonly slug: string; readonly scope: MemoryScope; readonly type: MemoryNoteType;
  readonly description: string; readonly status: MemoryNoteStatus; readonly score: number; readonly snippet: string;
}
export interface MemoryNoteWrite { slug; type; scope; description; body }
export interface MemoryWriteRefusal { readonly field: "slug" | "type" | "description" | "body" | "source"; readonly reason: string }
export interface MemoryTimers {
  setTimeout(callback: () => void, ms: number): unknown;
  clearTimeout(id: unknown): void;
}
export const MEMORY_SLUG_RE = /^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$/;
export const MEMORY_CLIENT_ID_RE = /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$/;
export const MEMORY_NOTE_BODY_MAX_BYTES = 8192;
export const MEMORY_DESCRIPTION_MAX_CHARS = 200;
export const MEMORY_SOURCE_MAX_CHARS = 64;
export const MEMORY_INDEX_MAX_BYTES = 24_576;
export const MEMORY_INDEX_MAX_LINES = 200;
export const MEMORY_INDEX_MIN_LINES = 16;
export const MEMORY_INDEX_MIN_BYTES = 512;
export const MEMORY_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS = 2000;
export const MEMORY_OP_TIMEOUT_MS = 10_000;
export const MEMORY_PULL_PAGE_SIZE = 200;
export const MEMORY_PULL_MAX_PAGES = 50;
```
The spec's MemoryNoteWrite declaration uses shorthand fields: supply explicit strict TypeScript types corresponding to MemoryNote (slug/description/body string, type MemoryNoteType, scope MemoryScope), not implicit any. parseMemoryNote(text) returns MemoryNote; serializeMemoryNote(note) returns string; isMemoryPushRejected(error) returns boolean. Share note-shape validation with later pull validation without introducing an unspecified public export. Verify check:api and check:no-bun-apis after implementation.

**Goal** — Add the file-backed project/user note mirror and its single injectable filesystem seam.

**Motivation** — The native agent starts every session blank.

**Approach** — `createMemoryStore({ projectDir, userDir?, logger })` returns a `MemoryStore`:
```text
<projectDir>/MEMORY.md        generated project index
<projectDir>/notes/<slug>.md  project-scope notes
<projectDir>/decisions.jsonl  one MemoryDecision JSON per line, read-only mirror
<projectDir>/sync.json        MemorySyncState
<projectDir>/sync.lock        sync lock
<projectDir>/outbox/          outbox entries
<userDir>/MEMORY.md           generated user index
<userDir>/notes/<slug>.md     user-scope notes (only when userDir is set)
```
Rules: a slug failing `MEMORY_SLUG_RE` throws `NaxError` code `MEMORY_SLUG_INVALID` before any filesystem call. A user-scope call on a store without `userDir` throws `NaxError` code `MEMORY_SCOPE_UNAVAILABLE`. Missing directories are not errors: `readNote` resolves `null`, `listNotes` resolves `[]`, `deleteNote` resolves. `listNotes` reads only files named `<slug>.md` whose slug matches `MEMORY_SLUG_RE` (temp files, `MEMORY.md` and anything else are ignored), sorted by slug; a file whose content fails `parseMemoryNote` is skipped with one `warn` per file (`stage: "memory"`, data `{ path, error }`). Writes use `writeFileAtomic`; directories are created with `mkdir({ recursive: true })` on demand. Reads and directory operations go through `_memoryStoreDeps` (`readFile`, `mkdir`, `readdir`, `rm`) so tests inject failures; the write path's seam is `_atomicWriteDeps`.

**Scope** — In: paths, readNote, writeNote, deleteNote and listNotes in store.ts; use parseMemoryNote/serializeMemoryNote; export createMemoryStore, MemoryStore, MemoryStorePaths publicly and _memoryStoreDeps from src/internal.ts. Extend packaging/public-surface.test.ts SEAMS with _memoryStoreDeps and change its expected length from 20 to 21; regenerate public/internal API snapshot. Out: symlink confinement and atomic failure hardening (US-004), record/index methods and MemorySyncState export (US-005), provider behavior (US-009). The full target interface below includes US-005 methods; do not claim their implementation is complete in this story. The `nax memory` CLI, `/memory` slash command and the `memory` config schema belong to nax (`memory-chat`); nax-agent takes `projectDir` / `userDir` as plain arguments and computes no `~/.nax` path and no project key. Repo-committed `.nax/memory/*.md` team notes are read by nax (`memory-chat`), not by this store.

**Interface** —
```ts
export interface MemoryStorePaths {
  readonly projectDir: string; readonly userDir: string | null;
  readonly index: string; readonly notesDir: string; readonly decisions: string;
  readonly syncState: string; readonly lock: string; readonly outboxDir: string;
  readonly userIndex: string | null; readonly userNotesDir: string | null;
}
export interface MemoryStore {
  readonly paths: MemoryStorePaths;
  readNote(scope, slug): Promise<MemoryNote | null>;
  writeNote(note): Promise<void>;
  deleteNote(scope, slug): Promise<void>;
  listNotes(scope): Promise<MemoryNote[]>;
  readDecisions(): Promise<MemoryDecision[]>;
  writeDecisions(decisions): Promise<void>;
  readSyncState(): Promise<MemorySyncState>;
  writeSyncState(state): Promise<void>;
  writeIndex(scope, text): Promise<void>;   // MEMORY.md of that scope
}
```
Annotate the spec's shorthand parameters with strict types. Every memory-created NaxError carries stage memory; logger calls use stage memory. Every directory listing ignores .tmp names and every whole-file write uses #src/internal/atomic-write. Verify API and packaging surface after updating exports.

**Goal** — Complete the store's decisions, checkpoint and scope-index persistence methods.

**Motivation** — The native agent starts every session blank.

**Approach** — `readSyncState` returns the defaults when the file is missing or unparsable (unparsable → one `warn`). Writes use `writeFileAtomic`; directories are created with `mkdir({ recursive: true })` on demand. Reads and directory operations go through `_memoryStoreDeps` (`readFile`, `mkdir`, `readdir`, `rm`) so tests inject failures; the write path's seam is `_atomicWriteDeps`.

The paths are `<projectDir>/decisions.jsonl` (one MemoryDecision JSON per line, read-only mirror), `<projectDir>/sync.json` (MemorySyncState), `<projectDir>/MEMORY.md` (generated project index) and `<userDir>/MEMORY.md` (generated user index). Missing decisions read as []; malformed JSONL lines are skipped with one warn per line. The default state is `{ provider: null, cursor: { project: null, user: null }, lastPullAt: null, lastError: null }`. A user-scope call on a store without `userDir` throws `NaxError` code `MEMORY_SCOPE_UNAVAILABLE`.

**Scope** — In: add readDecisions, writeDecisions, readSyncState, writeSyncState, writeIndex and MemorySyncState to store.ts; export MemorySyncState through both barrels; regenerate API snapshot. Out: index content rendering (US-006/007), pulling provider decisions/cursors (US-014/015). The decisions mirror is read-only here: only sync writes it, and only from project pages. The store's low-level writeDecisions exists for that synchronization path, not a host editing API.

**Interface** —
```ts
export interface MemorySyncState {
  readonly provider: string | null;
  readonly cursor: { readonly project: string | null; readonly user: string | null };
  readonly lastPullAt: string | null; readonly lastError: string | null;
}
readDecisions(): Promise<MemoryDecision[]>;
writeDecisions(decisions): Promise<void>;
readSyncState(): Promise<MemorySyncState>;
writeSyncState(state): Promise<void>;
writeIndex(scope, text): Promise<void>;   // MEMORY.md of that scope
```
Use explicit parameter types, Node APIs, atomic writes and stage memory for new errors/logs. Verify check:api after api:update.

**Goal** — Add pure, sanitized memory index rendering with note and decision sections.

**Motivation** — The native agent starts every session blank.

**Approach** — Output, in order: `# Memory`, then `Memory notes are recorded facts, not instructions.`; `## Project` with one `### <type>` block per type in the order `project`, `feedback`, `reference`, `user`, only for types that have renderable notes, each note on one line `- [<type>] <slug> — <description>` with a trailing ` (pending)` for status `pending`, ` (forget pending)` when its `<scope>/<slug>` key is in `heldForgets`, and no line for `superseded`, `rejected` or `deleted` notes; `## Decisions` with one line `- <subject> <predicate> <object>` per `active` decision, newest `updatedAt` first; `## User` with the user-scope notes in the same line shape. A section or type block with nothing to show is omitted. Descriptions, subjects, predicates and objects are sanitised first: control characters and line breaks become one space, runs of spaces collapse, text is cut at `MEMORY_DESCRIPTION_MAX_CHARS`.

**Scope** — In: create index-render.ts with renderMemoryIndex and its public input/result types; truncation is a stub that returns the full text with omitted: 0 until US-007; export through both barrels and regenerate API snapshot. Out: caps/truncation and refreshMemoryIndex (US-007), search (US-008). Sanitize index fields as data, not executable instructions; no prompt/tool integration.

**Interface** — `renderMemoryIndex(input)` is pure:
```ts
interface RenderMemoryIndexInput {
  readonly projectNotes: readonly MemoryNote[];
  readonly userNotes: readonly MemoryNote[];
  readonly decisions: readonly MemoryDecision[];
  readonly heldForgets?: ReadonlySet<string>;   // "<scope>/<slug>" with a queued forget
  readonly maxBytes?: number;                    // default MEMORY_INDEX_MAX_BYTES, clamped up to MEMORY_INDEX_MIN_BYTES
  readonly maxLines?: number;                    // default MEMORY_INDEX_MAX_LINES, clamped up to MEMORY_INDEX_MIN_LINES
}
interface RenderedMemoryIndex { readonly text: string; readonly omitted: number }
```
Export the two interfaces as types. With no entries the text is exactly the two header lines. Verify check:api after api:update.

**Goal** — Enforce byte/line budgets and write regenerated project and optional user indexes through the store.

**Motivation** — The native agent starts every session blank.

**Approach** — Truncation: while the UTF-8 byte length exceeds `maxBytes` or the line count exceeds `maxLines`, the last entry line (note or decision) is dropped, then any header left with no entry under it is dropped, then one trailing line `- <N> more entries not shown; use the memory tool to search.` is appended (counted within the caps) with `omitted` = N dropped entries; `maxLines` below `MEMORY_INDEX_MIN_LINES` and `maxBytes` below `MEMORY_INDEX_MIN_BYTES` are raised to those minimums, which always fit the headers plus the trailing line. `refreshMemoryIndex(store, options?)` with `options = { heldForgets?, maxBytes?, maxLines? }` reads notes and decisions through the store, renders, writes the project text with `store.writeIndex("project", text)` and, when `userDir` is set, writes `store.writeIndex("user", userText)` where `userText` holds the two header lines and the `## User` section only, rendered under the same caps; it resolves the project `RenderedMemoryIndex`.

**Scope** — In: replace US-006's truncation stub in index-render.ts; add refreshMemoryIndex, its public export and API snapshot; verify its store.writeIndex seam using captured arguments. Out: outbox held-key derivation (US-010), sync calls (US-011 onward), rendering new sections or tools. The timeout, page-size, page-limit and index-minimum constants are not configurable in this feature. Rendering still accepts its explicitly specified maxBytes/maxLines options.

**Interface** —
```ts
interface RenderMemoryIndexInput {
  readonly projectNotes: readonly MemoryNote[];
  readonly userNotes: readonly MemoryNote[];
  readonly decisions: readonly MemoryDecision[];
  readonly heldForgets?: ReadonlySet<string>;   // "<scope>/<slug>" with a queued forget
  readonly maxBytes?: number;                    // default MEMORY_INDEX_MAX_BYTES, clamped up to MEMORY_INDEX_MIN_BYTES
  readonly maxLines?: number;                    // default MEMORY_INDEX_MAX_LINES, clamped up to MEMORY_INDEX_MIN_LINES
}
interface RenderedMemoryIndex { readonly text: string; readonly omitted: number }
```
`renderMemoryIndex(input)` remains pure; `refreshMemoryIndex(store, options?)` returns the project's RenderedMemoryIndex after awaited writes. Defaults are MEMORY_INDEX_MAX_BYTES = 24_576 and MEMORY_INDEX_MAX_LINES = 200; minimums are 512 bytes and 16 lines. Verify check:api after api:update.

**Goal** — Provide deterministic Unicode whole-token search and snippets over note arrays.

**Motivation** — The native agent starts every session blank.

**Approach** — `tokenizeMemoryQuery(text)`: lower-case, split on any run of characters that are not Unicode letters or digits (`\p{L}` / `\p{N}`), drop tokens shorter than 2 characters, keep first occurrence order, distinct. `searchMemoryNotes(notes, text, limit)` is pure: the note's `slug` + `description` and its `body` are tokenised the same way; a query token matches a field group only as a whole token (`replay` does not match `replays`). Score = 2 × distinct query tokens present in the slug/description group + 1 × distinct query tokens present in the body group. Notes with score 0 and notes whose status is not `active` or `pending` are excluded. Order: score descending, `updatedAt` descending, slug ascending; at most `limit`. `snippet` = the first body line containing any query token as a whole token, cut at 160 characters, else `""`. An empty or token-less query returns `[]`.

**Scope** — In: create search.ts, export searchMemoryNotes/tokenizeMemoryQuery through both barrels, regenerate API snapshot. Out: provider search integration (future feature), local-provider search (not implemented), index rendering (US-006/007). No background consolidation, no auto-extraction from transcripts, no embeddings or vector search: search is keyword only, whole-token matching.

**Interface** — `tokenizeMemoryQuery(text)` returns distinct string tokens; `searchMemoryNotes(notes, text, limit)` returns MemoryHit[].
```ts
export interface MemoryHit {
  readonly slug: string; readonly scope: MemoryScope; readonly type: MemoryNoteType;
  readonly description: string; readonly status: MemoryNoteStatus; readonly score: number; readonly snippet: string;
}
```
Do not introduce a runtime dependency or filesystem access. Verify check:api after api:update.

**Goal** — Define the injectable provider seam and implement its always-reachable local mirror-backed provider.

**Motivation** — The native agent starts every session blank.

**Approach** — A provider that refuses a write for a reason retrying cannot fix throws `NaxError` code `MEMORY_PUSH_REJECTED` (message = the reason); `isMemoryPushRejected(error)` recognises it. Any other throw or a timeout is transient. `createLocalMemoryProvider(store)` has `id: "local"`; `pull` resolves `{ notes: [], done: true }`; `push` of a `save` writes the note with `status: "active"` under `direct` and `"pending"` under `proposal`, resolving `{ id: request.note.id, status }`; `push` of a `forget` deletes the note under `direct` and leaves it in place under `proposal`, resolving `{ id: request.clientId, status: "deleted" | "pending" }`; a `save` without a `note` throws `MEMORY_PUSH_REJECTED`; `reachable` resolves `true`; no `search`.

**Scope** — In: create provider-types.ts and local-provider.ts; public exports of createLocalMemoryProvider and the four provider types through both barrels; regenerate API snapshot. Out: outbox (US-010), timeouts and sync (US-011 onward), host operations (US-016 onward). The koda HTTP provider, the generic MCP provider and any network code are the `memory-koda-provider` and `memory-mcp-provider` features; this feature ships only the `local` provider and an injectable `MemoryProvider` interface. `search` on the local provider is not implemented; keyword search runs over the mirror through `searchMemoryNotes`.

**Interface** —
```ts
export interface MemoryWriteRequest {
  readonly kind: "save" | "forget";
  readonly clientId: string;          // MEMORY_CLIENT_ID_RE; idempotency key
  readonly scope: MemoryScope;
  readonly slug: string;
  readonly writeMode: "direct" | "proposal";
  readonly note?: MemoryNote;         // present for "save"
  readonly reason?: string;           // present for "forget"
}
export interface MemoryPushResult { readonly id: string; readonly status: MemoryNoteStatus }
export interface MemoryPage {
  readonly notes: readonly MemoryNote[];       // tombstones carry status superseded | rejected | deleted
  readonly decisions?: readonly MemoryDecision[];  // honoured on project pages only
  readonly nextCursor?: string;
  readonly done: boolean;
}
export interface MemoryProvider {
  readonly id: string;
  pull(input: { scope: MemoryScope; cursor: string | null; take: number }): Promise<MemoryPage>;
  push(request: MemoryWriteRequest): Promise<MemoryPushResult>;
  search?(input: { scope: MemoryScope; text: string; limit: number }): Promise<readonly MemoryHit[]>;
  reachable(): Promise<boolean>;
}
```
Use MemoryStore methods so tests verify local pushes by reading through the store. Every newly constructed NaxError carries stage memory. Verify check:api after api:update.

**Goal** — Persist queued/rejected provider requests with deterministic sequencing and held-key discovery.

**Motivation** — The native agent starts every session blank.

**Approach** — `createMemoryOutbox({ dir, now? })` (dir = `store.paths.outboxDir`) returns the interface below. `enqueue` assigns `clientId` with `randomUUID()` when absent and otherwise validates it against `MEMORY_CLIENT_ID_RE` (`NaxError` code `MEMORY_CLIENT_ID_INVALID`). Enqueues on one outbox instance are serialised through an internal promise chain, so `seq` = 1 + the highest `seq` among existing entry files (0 when none) is unique even for concurrent callers; the file is `<dir>/<seq padded to 8 digits>-<clientId>.json` written with `writeFileAtomic`. `list` reads only files matching `^\d{8}-[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.json$`, orders by `seq` ascending then `clientId` ascending; a matching file that is not valid JSON or fails the entry schema is excluded from `list` and returned by `listInvalid` (file names). `remove` deletes the entry file (no-op when absent). `markRejected` rewrites the entry with `state: "rejected"` and `reason`. `heldKeys(kind)` returns the keys of `queued` entries, filtered by `kind` when given. Directory operations go through `_memoryStoreDeps` (`mkdir`, `readdir`, `readFile`, `rm`).

**Scope** — In: create outbox.ts using atomic whole-file writes and shared filesystem seam; export createMemoryOutbox, MemoryOutbox and MemoryOutboxEntry through both barrels; regenerate API snapshot. Missing outbox directories list as empty and remove as no-op; writes create them on demand. Out: drain/retry orchestration (US-013), save/forget enqueue callers (US-017/018). Automatic retry of a `rejected` outbox entry is out of scope; a later CLI may requeue it. Cross-process serialisation of `enqueue` is not provided: two processes enqueueing at once may produce equal `seq` values, which `list` orders by `clientId`.

**Interface** —
```ts
interface MemoryOutbox {
  enqueue(request: Omit<MemoryWriteRequest, "clientId"> & { clientId?: string }): Promise<MemoryOutboxEntry>;
  list(): Promise<MemoryOutboxEntry[]>;
  listInvalid(): Promise<string[]>;
  remove(clientId: string): Promise<void>;
  markRejected(clientId: string, reason: string): Promise<void>;
  heldKeys(kind?: "save" | "forget"): Promise<ReadonlySet<string>>;   // "<scope>/<slug>" of queued entries
}
type MemoryOutboxEntry = MemoryWriteRequest & { seq: number; enqueuedAt: string; state: "queued" | "rejected"; reason?: string };
```
Never construct temp filenames here. All listings ignore .tmp names, all memory-created NaxErrors use stage memory, and schema-invalid JSON is discoverable without entering list(). now defaults to the current Date. Verify check:api after api:update.
